    {
      "id": "claim_9bcfe5e2b4424930a3e26197e2a9155b",
      "statement": "Backend and frontend rollouts on both stacks follow the same flow: docker compose pull, then up -d --force-recreate --no-deps inside a 5-attempt retry loop with 5s sleeps (a racing deploy or an interrupted removal makes compose fail with 'removal of container … is already in progress', which is transient and converges on retry), a wait for the container to answer docker exec echo ok, and disk reclaim via docker image prune -af --filter 'until=72h' — the -a plus until filter keeps current and recent rollback tags, where plain prune -f only removes dangling images.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L144-L164",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce73e994f6edbafe03fb98ff8275944edf810a61ec9392872c37e1a9549fc861:"
